SUMMARY:The Sentence and book exchange
DESCRIPTION:Petaluma Book (And Brew) Club\nPlease bring 5 books you’d like to exchange. Any books you do not want returned may be left with us\, and we will donate them to the Friends of the Library book sale.\n\nThe Sentence is a 2021 novel by Louise Erdrich\, a ghost story set in a Minneapolis bookstore from November 2019 to November 2020\, during the pandemic and George Floyd protests. It follows Tookie\, a Native American woman recently released from prison\, who is haunted by the ghost of an annoying customer\, Flora\, and must unravel the mystery while navigating personal challenges and a year of national turmoil. The book explores themes of grief\, racism\, addiction\, and family\, blending humor with profound reflection on what is owed to the living and the dead.
